<header><p class="enc-kicker">Historical factor</p><h1 class="enc-title">Drought and climate change</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Drought and climate change refers to environmental shifts, such as prolonged droughts, cooling or failing <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/monsoon">monsoons</a>, that undermined harvests, pastures and state revenues. Such pressures are linked to the collapse of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/akkadian-empire">Akkadian Empire</a>, the decline of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khmer-empire">Khmer Empire</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ming-empire">Ming Empire</a>, and the weakening of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xiongnu-empire">Xiongnu Empire</a> through droughts and catastrophic winters.</p></div>
